# the UseResolver says nothing about 'whatever', 'deeply' or 'nested': the
# right side of a dot is a member of whatever the left side turns out to be,
# and sending it through the scope chain would find a global of that name in
# silence. It reports 'missing' alone, which is the one name written in a
# position a scope can answer for.
#
# The typer speaks too, and it is a different sentence: 'i32 has no member
# named ...'. Both halves in one golden is the point -- the second one only
# started appearing when an expression written as a statement began to be
# typed at all, on 2026-09-02
def main : i32
    let thing = 1
    thing.whatever
    thing.deeply.nested
    missing.field
    return 0
